# SMP post stage 0x1C0918..0x1C0A70 driven live: constant bus words through the real audio interrupt.
# `irq 17 break=0x1c0918` stops the interrupt before the post stage, the pokes put bus words on
# DM(0x9404E..) (the voice bus; the interrupt does not clear them), `resume` finishes it. The gate
# words DM(0x9403E, 42, 46 (+1)) are what the ARM writes as 1.0 for the piano ids (arm-organ-messages);
# their smoothed states DM(0x94040, 44, 48 (+1)) start open here. Result: ring[0] -> bus * 2^-29
# (steady state gain 1.0, 0.938 after 300 interrupts, one-pole constant 0.99 per interrupt).
# docs/research/piano-bus-convention.md s2.  Run: sharc-ref smp.bin tools/oracle_scenarios/smp_post_stage.scn --out target/oracle/post
meta rate 48000
warmup 0x1c11e0 100000 flag12=1
poke 0x5201 0x40
fifo 0x92196
irq 13
poke 0x9268B 0
poke 0x9268A 0
poke 0x94040 f1.0
poke 0x94041 f1.0
poke 0x94044 f1.0
poke 0x94045 f1.0
poke 0x94048 f1.0
poke 0x94049 f1.0
poke 0x9403e f1.0
poke 0x9403f f1.0
poke 0x94042 f1.0
poke 0x94043 f1.0
poke 0x94046 f1.0
poke 0x94047 f1.0
loop 300
irq 17 break=0x1c0918
poke 0x9404E 0x20000000
poke 0x9404F 0x20000000
resume
capture ring 0xB2000 12
end
